-- title:
--   Finite Lebesgue measure is dominated by the exponential product class
-- statement:
--   Let $\lambda$ be the strictly positive exponential-density measure used in the construction. In every finite dimension $n$,
--   $$\operatorname{Leb}_{\mathbb R^n}\ll\lambda^{\otimes n}.$$
--   Together with the converse domination, this identifies the two finite-dimensional measure classes and permits invariance statements to be transported in either direction.
-- source:
--   Ruijun Wang, Comparisons of benchmark equivalence relations, Theorem 1.5 (formerly MeasureEquivalence.tex, Theorem 1.3); supporting declaration MeasureEquivalenceRestrictedProduct.finite_volume_ac_exponential in RestrictedFiniteNull.lean, lines 39–58; local source SHA-256 44815bfba096cf9a82c996edf04a3b3a2ac2e8b7c9d9b8ea541c39e43229047f. Designated upload repository: https://github.com/RayjunWang/Benchmark (no source commit published yet).

